    "text": "By currents ,\n1 days ago Each spring across Lakeland, crape myrtle trees are often cut back to thick, bare stubs in a practice widely referred to as “crape murder.” Although many homeowners believe this aggressive pruning encourages stronger growth, horticulture experts warn that it can actually harm the tree over time. Wesley Wright,... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
